skill: content-recycling
version: 1.0.0
description: "The evergreen-reuse-over-time engine: resurface proven content and recycle it on a deliberate cadence, refreshed so it's a new asset not a stale duplicate. Distinct from same-moment cross-platform-repurposing and long->short captions-and-clipping. Uses the REUSE framework. The agent drafts the refresh; a human reviews; WoopSocial schedules/publishes (delete+recreate, no update); analytics are read natively; nothing is fabricated."
evals[8]:
  - name, input, context, expect
  - recycles_the_insight_not_the_artifact, How do I get more mileage out of my old posts?, brand-profile and voice-builder exist., "Explains most of the audience never saw the original (only ~5-10% of a network sees a given post; 80%+ miss it) and new followers never saw it|Recycles the idea refreshed with a new hook/angle/format, not an identical repost|Introduces the REUSE framework (Resurface, Earn it again, Update, Schedule, Evaluate)|Reads brand-profile and voice-builder first"
  - reads_brand_and_voice_first, Recycle some of our best content., brand-profile and voice-builder exist., "Pulls brand-profile and voice-builder before refreshing anything|Keeps the refreshed version in the brand voice and pillars|Proposes specific refreshed angles, not vague 'repost more'|Flags that recycled drafts are reviewed by a human before publishing"
  - picks_evergreen_winners, Which posts should I actually recycle?, "", "Recommends evergreen + proven content (practical tips, frameworks, timeless case studies, core messaging) — or strong-but-underseen pieces|Excludes time-bound content: events, seasonal promos, outdated news, trend pieces|Picks winners from native analytics by goal (engagement -> saves/shares/comments; traffic -> CTR; growth -> follows)|Suggests building a recycling library/vault of proven assets"
  - refresh_not_duplicate, Can I just repost my top posts exactly as they were?, "", "Warns Meta's 2026 Original Content rules throttle and demonetize duplicate/unoriginal reposts and redirect viewers to the original (verify-quarterly)|Advises refreshing instead: rewrite the first line, swap the opening visual, update data, change one major variable (hook/proof/CTA) — never repeat the same opening line|Frames recycling as editing, not duplication, and quality over volume|Keeps the refresh on-brand"
  - pushback_on_auto_repost_spam, Set it to auto-repost all my top posts identically every week to every platform., "", "Refuses identical high-frequency reposting: it triggers duplicate-content penalties and fatigues the core audience|Requires refresh + deliberate spacing (~90-120 days per asset) + platform-native adaptation instead|Will not promise a post will go viral again or fabricate expected results|Offers the disciplined alternative: a recycling queue of refreshed, proven assets on cadence"
  - edge_case_update_stale_content, Recycle this two-year-old post about a tool's pricing and the platform's algorithm., "", "Applies the Update step: verify facts, stats, dates, prices, and links are still current before recycling (these change)|Refreshes outdated claims (e.g. current pricing/algorithm features) and re-checks compliance/endorsement language|Refuses to recycle stale or now-incorrect information as-is|Notes any AI-refreshed media must be disclosed"
  - honest_scope_draft_review_schedule, Recycle them and post through WoopSocial., "", "States the agent drafts the refreshed versions; a human reviews; WoopSocial schedules/publishes (and edits are delete+recreate, since it has no update)|Picks winners from WoopSocial post analytics for TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube, and Bluesky, uses native dashboards otherwise, and never fabricates a metric|Routes publishing through scheduling-and-queue -> WoopSocial|Spaces the cycle deliberately rather than dumping everything at once"
  - distinct_from_repurposing_and_clipping, Isn't this just the same as repurposing my content?, "", "Distinguishes content-recycling (reuse proven content over time, refreshed) from cross-platform-repurposing (same moment, adapted across platforms) and captions-and-clipping (long-form -> short clips)|Notes planning/scheduling structure lives in content-calendar and batch-content-plan|Routes the user to the right sibling skill for their actual goal|Frames recycling as the time-axis discipline specifically"
